Sliding window with a last-seen index map. Move the left edge to one past the previous occurrence of the current character, then track the max window length.

```js
function longestUniqueRun(s) {
  const last = new Map();
  let left = 0, best = 0;
  for (let right = 0; right < s.length; right++) {
    const ch = s[right];
    if (last.has(ch) && last.get(ch) >= left) {
      left = last.get(ch) + 1;
    }
    last.set(ch, right);
    best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);
  }
  return best;
}
```

O(n) time, O(min(n, alphabet)) space. Empty string returns 0 since the loop never runs.

Sliding window with a last-seen index map. Move the right pointer, and when a character repeats inside the window, jump the left pointer past its previous position. Track the max window length as you go.

```js
function longestUniqueRun(s) {
  const last = new Map();
  let left = 0, best = 0;
  for (let right = 0; right < s.length; right++) {
    const ch = s[right];
    if (last.has(ch) && last.get(ch) >= left) {
      left = last.get(ch) + 1;
    }
    last.set(ch, right);
    best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);
  }
  return best;
}
```

O(n) time, O(min(n, alphabet)) space. Empty string returns 0 naturally.

